{
  "title": "A fixed-frequency clock test does not separate the 19.48-hour KIC 10001893 signal in 14 Kepler quarters",
  "abstract": "We compare fixed-frequency sine fits in barycentric and spacecraft time for KIC 10001893 in 14 Kepler release 25 quarters. At 14.261300 microHz, fitted waveforms differ by only 0.15 to 0.28 ppm RMS. Conditional six-day residual sign trials select each clock about half the time. Small observed spacecraft-time preferences lie within both trial ranges. A strong 210.6816 microHz pulsation separates the clocks in later quarters, but its full-record fit shows limits of a constant-sinusoid model. The weak signal cannot identify a clock or a physical cause under this test. No planet or new source is confirmed. Code, input hashes, aggregate results, a figure and external-scratch retrieval steps are included.",
